Note that we are asked which of the following MUST be true, not COULD be true. For such kind of questions if you can prove that a statement is NOT true for one particular set of numbers, it will mean that this statement is not always true and hence not a correct answer.
So we should try to make the listed statements not true for some r and y (which satisfy y≠3 and 2r/y=prime>2).
I. r = y --> not necessarily true: r=3 and y=2 (2r/y=3=prime>2);
II. y=1 --> not necessarily true: r=3 and y=2 (2r/y=3=prime>2);
III. r and y are prime integers --> not necessarily true: r=10 and y=4 (2r/y=5=prime>2).
Answer: A.

