reasoning:
Let the time when all three were working together be t hours. Then:
Tom worked for t+4 hour and has done 1/16*(t+4) part of the job;
Peter worked for t+2 hour and has done 1/8*(t+2) part of the job;
John worked for t hours and has done 1/4*t part of the job:
1/16*(t+4)+1/8*(t+2)+1/4*t=1 --> multiply by 16 --> (t+4)+(2t+2)+4t=16 --> t=10/7;
Hence Peter has done 1/8*(10/7+2)=1/8 *24/7=3/7
Answer: E

Let the rate of outlet pipe be x liters/hour;
Rate of inlet pipe is 8 litres/min, or 8*60 = 480 liters/hour;
Net outflow rate when both pipes operate would be x-480 liters/hour.
Capacity of the tank = x*8 hours = (x-480)*(8+4) hours
8x=(x-480)*12 --> x=1440 --> capacity = 8x = 11520 liters.
Answer: D.
